diff --git a/crates/rightkit-qa/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-qa/CHANGELOG.md
index cae4c18..3442a9e 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-qa/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-qa/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.6.5 (unreleased)
+
+Additive; nothing is breaking. Not built or run locally; CI is the compiler.
+
+- **Fake CLI fixtures (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#382).** New `fake_cli` module and `rightkit-fake-cli` binary: a scriptable fake command-line process (a model CLI such as Claude Code or Codex, or a command-line editor engine) driven by a JSON script. Rules match on arguments, stdin and environment; responses carry stdout, stderr, JSON stdout with templated leaves, streamed chunks, files written, delays, hangs, a heartbeat grandchild and an exit code; `record` appends one JSON line per invocation. `fake_cli::run`, `decide` and `perform` serve a multiplexing test binary. Tests: `tests/fake_cli.rs` and the module's own. A framed-stdio sidecar engine is not faked.
+- **Isolated native-real mode and run isolation (#752, #468).** New `isolation` module, compiled only with debug assertions: `native_real_mode`, `native_qa_enabled`, `qa_data_dir`, `qa_subdir`, `native_real_env` (refuses a relative, root, home or parent-of-home run root), `refuse_in_native_real`, `engine_isolation_env` / `engine_isolation_env_for` (child engine `HOME`, suite, Windows profile), `webview_data_dir`, `webview_store_id`, `MUTE_MEDIA_SCRIPT`, `dialog_answer_js`, `DIALOG_SEAM_TS`. Browser half: `@rightkit/qa/dialog`.
+- **Control crawler, inventory and parity report (#427).** New `crawl` module: `CRAWL_JS`, `crawl_section`, `Inventory` / `SectionInventory` / `ControlEntry` (JSON read and write), `compare_inventories` with `ParityOptions` and `ParityReport` (`is_pass`, `to_markdown`). New scenario step `ui_crawl` (`section`, `path`, `min_controls`) writes a section as evidence. `@rightkit/qa` produces the same JSON.
+- **Legal gate helper (#387).** New `legal_gate` module: `LegalGate` and `Control::accept_legal_gate`. (Failure evidence, the page-error recorder, `click_until`, `live_log_path`, `log_tail`, the `command` `args` fix and public `strip_verbatim` were already on main.)
+- **Interval detectors (#355).** `media::parse_detect_intervals` with `DetectFilter` (ffmpeg `blackdetect`, `freezedetect`, `silencedetect` logs to `Interval`s); `loudness::loudness_series` (`SeriesWindow::Momentary` or `ShortTerm`, `LoudnessPoint`) and `loudness::loudness_outside`. The pure-PCM and pure-frame detectors were already on main.
+- **PostRight gap (#249, item 7).** A `[engine].data_dir_env` that names `RIGHTKIT_SUITE_ROOT` is no longer added to a UI launch (the launch owns it), instead of being refused as an override of a harness-owned value. Test: `scenario::tests`.
+- **No backup copy (#771 D1).** `inplace::swap_in_place` and `replace_file_in_place`, and so the QA binary stash and the macOS QA bundle, keep no `.previous`: the old copy waits under a transient `<name>.swap-<pid>` during the swap and is deleted (renamed back on failure), and a stale `<name>.previous` is deleted. `inplace::previous_path` remains only to name that stale copy.
+- Not changed: #678 (UI background proof fails on the Dell). It needs the failing run's evidence on that host.
+
 ## 0.6.4 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Fixed (rightkit#358, ledger 189): `set_viewport` no longer reports before the size settles. It confirms two consecutive non-empty page readings 500 ms apart (`SETTLE_INTERVAL`), even when the window already has the requested size; an unsettled readback or a placement timeout now returns `ok:false` with an `error`, and `Control::set_viewport` rejects a reply that is not `settled:true` with `placementTimedOut:false`. Hidden macOS windows keep their `constrainFrameRect:toScreen:` exemption (a window-owned Objective-C association, no class swap) through deferred AppKit layout, are reapplied inside the settle bound, and must reach the requested size; showing the window restores normal constraints. New public `embedded::set_viewport` and `ViewportWindow::requires_exact_size` (default `false`; additive). Tests: `tests/viewport.rs` (feature `control`), viewport unit tests, macOS constraint test. The `rightkit-qa-driver` native qualification test from the same patch is not applied here.
