--- a/crates/rightkit-qa/README.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-qa/README.md
@@ -310,3 +310,23 @@ let report = run_suite(&cfg, &SuiteOptions { hooks, ..Default::default() })?;
 ```
 
 A custom step's return value feeds `[[step.expect]]` and `save` like a built-in's. `util::hmac_sha256` and `util::secret_forms` (with base64 at all three stream alignments) are available to mocks and secret-absence steps.
+
+## Fake CLI and fake engine fixtures
+
+`fake_cli` and the `rightkit-fake-cli` binary fake a model CLI (Claude Code, Codex) or a command-line editor engine from a JSON script, instead of a bespoke fake per app. Point the app's "tool path" setting at the binary, with the script in `RIGHTKIT_FAKE_CLI_SCRIPT` or as the leading `--fake-cli-script <file>` argument; or call `fake_cli::run` from your own multiplexing test binary and `decide` / `perform` to post-process a response. The script format (rules matched on arguments, stdin and environment; templated stdout, JSON, streamed chunks, files written, delays, hangs, a heartbeat grandchild, an invocation record) is documented at the top of `src/fake_cli.rs`. A framed-stdio sidecar engine is not faked here.
+
+## Isolated native-real runs (debug builds only)
+
+The `isolation` module (compiled only with debug assertions, so a release build cannot carry it) is what an app's QA-only code and a launcher share for a run on the real app with no real user data: `native_real_env(run_root)` is the launch environment (`RIGHTKIT_QA_NATIVE`, `RIGHTKIT_QA_NATIVE_REAL`, `RIGHTKIT_QA_DATA_DIR`, suite directories), refusing a relative, root, home or parent-of-home run root. In the app, `native_real_mode()` and `qa_data_dir()` read it back, `refuse_in_native_real` fails a credential-store, sign-in or sync path, `engine_isolation_env` gives a child engine its own `HOME` and Windows profile, `webview_data_dir` / `webview_store_id` give each run its own webview store, `MUTE_MEDIA_SCRIPT` silences media, and `dialog_answer_js` / `DIALOG_SEAM_TS` answer native file dialogs from the harness (the browser side is `@rightkit/qa/dialog`). Pass the environment through `LaunchSpec::env`; the paths must sit inside the QA home.
+
+## Control inventory and parity report
+
+`crawl::crawl_section(&control, "settings")` lists the interactive controls of the page the app shows (role, accessible name, enabled, visible, focusable, box); the `ui_crawl` scenario step does the same and writes the section as evidence. An `Inventory` holds the sections of one app on one platform and reads and writes JSON; `compare_inventories(&mac, &windows, &ParityOptions::default())` returns a `ParityReport` (controls only one side has, differing states, sections only one side crawled) with `to_markdown()`. `@rightkit/qa` writes and reads the same JSON.
+
+## Interval detectors and loudness over time
+
+`media::parse_detect_intervals` turns an ffmpeg `blackdetect`, `freezedetect` or `silencedetect` log into `Interval`s (the pure-PCM and pure-frame detectors `silence_intervals`, `black_intervals`, `freeze_intervals`, `clipped_runs` are the same shape). `loudness::loudness_series` gives momentary (400 ms) or short-term (3 s) loudness per 100 ms step and `loudness::loudness_outside` the spans outside a target range.
+
+## First-run legal gate
+
+`Control::accept_legal_gate(&LegalGate::default())` completes the RightKit legal gate through the real UI when it shows (individual, acknowledgement, "Agree & continue") and returns whether it was shown.
